# local env files — everything but the committed template.
#
# This was `.env*.local` + `.env` + `.env.prod`, which left anything else
# starting with `.env` trackable: a `.env.backup-…`, a `.env.dev`, a
# `.env.old` would all have been staged by `git add -A`, with their secrets.
# Deny by default and allow the one file that belongs in the repo.
.env*
!.env.example

